{"nodes": [{"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_demo_engine_advanced", "label": "Demo Engine Advanced Tutorial", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_importsolidworkssystem", "label": "chrono.ImportSolidWorksSystem", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Takes the module path without the .py suffix and with an explicit './' prefix even for the current directory; returns the exported items which the caller adds one by one to a ChSystemNSC."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_chpythonengine", "label": "ChPythonEngine::ImportSolidWorksSystem (C++)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "C++ cannot load the exported .py directly, so the PYTHON module is linked and ChPythonEngine performs the same import; every trick in the Python tutorial is reproducible from C++ through it."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_name_based_lookup", "label": "Name-based Object Lookup (SearchMarker / SearchBody)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The exported scene is addressed by mnemonic names rather than indices; SolidWorks coordinate-system features become ChMarker objects and parts become bodies. When unsure of a name, grep the exported .py for SetName(\"...\")."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_chlinkmotorrotationspeed", "label": "ChLinkMotorRotationSpeed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Actuation is added in Python because the exporter emits only mating constraints. Initialize() takes two bodies plus a ChFramed whose Z axis is the rotation axis; reusing a CAD-authored marker frame is preferred over typing rotation/position values by hand. SetSpindleConstraint() picks the connection type and SetMotorFunction() takes a ChFunction (ChFunctionConst for constant speed)."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_chpovrayassetcustom", "label": "ChPovRayAssetCustom", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-body appearance is injected as raw POVray statements attached as an asset, so the postprocessor emits them into the generated scripts without Chrono needing its own material model. SetCustomPOVcommandsScript() does the same at global scene scale (lights, ground plane, grid)."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_chbodyauxref_reference_frame", "label": "ChBodyAuxRef Reference Frame vs Center of Mass", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exported bodies are ChBodyAuxRef, not plain ChBody, because ChBody assumes the reference coordsys coincides with the center of mass while a CAD part's origin generally does not. The COG is computed by SolidWorks from the assigned material densities; for a rigid-solved subassembly the body reference is the subassembly origin."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_visual_debugging_overlays", "label": "Visual Debugging Overlays (SetShowLinks / SetShowCOGs / SetShowFrames)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Making every body 80% transparent first, then rendering constraint frames, COGs and body frames, turns POVray output into a visual debugger for the imported mechanism."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_attached_moving_camera", "label": "ChCamera Attached to a Moving Body", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Position and aim point are expressed in the carrying body's coordinate system, so the viewpoint rides along with the part (e.g. a driver's-eye view)."}], "edges": [{"source": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_demo_engine_advanced", "target": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_demo_engine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/tutorials/solidworks/demo_engine_advanced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_advanced_importsolidworkssystem", "target": "doxygen_documentation_tutorials_solidworks_demo_engine_assembly_to_python_export", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen